<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.1 PCT IN JANUARY - NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.1 PCT IN JANUARY - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 0.16</p>
<p>billion zlotys, or 0.1 percent, in January to 136.04 billion</p>
<p>after a 6.2 percent rise in December, preliminary central bank</p>
<p>figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     JAN     DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p>  Change vs pvs period (pct)	  0.1     6.2(5.9)	 1.1</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		 136.04  135.89(135.49) 105.46</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    24.26   23.37	    21.44</p>
<p>  National currency		   111.79  112.51(112.12)  84.02</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  22.77   23.56	    19.28</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  83.33   80.92(81.09)   56.98</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets.</p>
<p>Polish central bank announcement:</p>
<p>From January 1, 1997 the National Bank of Poland introduced</p>
<p>changes in methods of monetary aggregate calculation, to match</p>
<p>standards of international financial institutions. Therefore</p>
<p>December data will be verified after the bank receives balance</p>
<p>sheet information from commercial banks.</p>
<p>A full explanation of the introduced changes will be</p>
<p>published soon.   -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
